    "description": "LCA path aggregation; requires >>lca. _lca_path<policy,edge=true> defaults to directional edge values; edge=false stores vertex values with set(v,cost) or make(span<const cost>). Vertex mode add/addsol take only endpoints; make uses external indices [base,n], skips earlier entries, fills missing values with policy::id(), and ignores excess entries. Values start at policy::id() and survive build(root=-1); clear resets them. After changing topology or values, build again before any query. Policy requires node, cost, id(), lift(cost), and associative merge(node,node) with a two-sided identity; commutativity is unnecessary. query(a,b) follows a-to-b order and includes both endpoint vertices in vertex mode, counting the LCA once; disconnected endpoints return id(). query_up(v,k) follows v to ancestor(v,k), query_down(v,k) follows the reverse direction; require 0<=k<=depth(v). Both include endpoint vertices in vertex mode; k=0 returns the vertex value there, or id() in edge mode. bisect(a,b,f) returns the farthest vertex whose a-to-vertex aggregate passes f, or -1 for disconnected endpoints or no passing vertex prefix. It requires f(id())=true and prefix-monotonicity; in edge mode a is always accepted via the empty path. Queries and bisect take O(log n) assuming O(1) node copies, merge, and predicates; bisect uses O(log n) scratch space. Inherits subtree queries, temporary-root LCA queries, and it(f,rev=true)."
